.TH SCD-ENTRIES 1 "2026-11-10" "SCD Reporting 1.0.0" "SCD Reporting"
.SH NAME
scd\-entries \- list or export your own SCD Reporting entries
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scd\-entries
[\fB\-q\fR \fITEXT\fR] [\fB\-p\fR \fISLUG\fR]... [\fB\-\-category\fR \fISLUG\fR]... [\fB\-\-from\fR \fIDATE\fR] [\fB\-\-to\fR \fIDATE\fR] [\fB\-\-period\fR \fINAME\fR] [\fB\-\-archived\fR \fB0\fR|\fB1\fR|\fBall\fR] [\fB\-n\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-offset\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-all\-pages\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-f\fR \fIFORMAT\fR [\fB\-o\fR \fIFILE\fR | \fB\-O\fR]] [\fB\-c\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-u\fR \fIURL\fR] [\fB\-t\fR \fITOKEN\fR] [\fB\-\-token\-file\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fISEC\fR] [\fB\-\-ca\-bundle\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-k\fR] [\fB\-v\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists the entries you authored, the "My Entries" scope, through \fBGET /api/entries/\fR.
Any role may use it. Without \fB\-f\fR it prints a table of id, period, project slugs, flags
(\fBP\fRrivate, \fBC\fRritical, \fBH\fRighlight, \fBA\fRrchived) and title, newest period first.
With \fB\-f\fR it downloads \fIevery\fR matching entry in an export format (paging options are
ignored); exports are audited.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-q " TEXT" "\fR, \fP\-\-query " TEXT
Substring of the title, description or a tag name.
.TP
.BI \-p " SLUG" "\fR, \fP\-\-project " SLUG
Project slug or id. Repeatable; matches any.
.TP
.BI \-\-category " SLUG"
Category slug or id. Repeatable; matches any.
.TP
.BI \-\-from " DATE" "\fR, \fP\-\-to " DATE
Entries whose period \fIoverlaps\fR the range (unlike \fBscd\-report\fR, which defaults to containment).
.TP
.BI \-\-period " NAME"
\fBtoday\fR, \fBthis\-week\fR, \fBlast\-week\fR (weeks start Monday),
\fBthis\-month\fR, \fBlast\-month\fR, \fBthis\-quarter\fR, \fBlast\-quarter\fR
(calendar quarters), \fBthis\-year\fR, \fBlast\-year\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-archived " WHICH"
\fB0\fR current entries (default), \fB1\fR archived only, \fBall\fR both.
.TP
.BI \-n " N" "\fR, \fP\-\-limit " N
Rows per request, 1\(en1000 (default 50).
.TP
.BI \-\-offset " N"
Skip the first \fIN\fR matches.
.TP
.B \-\-all\-pages
Fetch every match, paging automatically.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the structured entry objects (ids, slugs and names of projects, categories, lab priorities,
group, entry type; tags; flags; timestamps; web URL) as a JSON array.
.TP
.BI \-f " FORMAT" "\fR, \fP\-\-format " FORMAT
Export instead of listing: \fBtxt\fR, \fBmd\fR, \fBcsv\fR, \fBjson\fR, \fBxlsx\fR or \fBpdf\fR.
.TP
.BI \-o " FILE" "\fR, \fP\-\-output " FILE
Write to \fIFILE\fR instead of standard output (\fB\-\fR means standard output).
.TP
.BR \-O ", " \-\-remote\-name
Write to the file name the server suggests (e.g. \fBscd_report_20261110_1432.md\fR) in the
current directory.
.SH CONNECTION OPTIONS
These override the environment, \fB.env\fR files and the config file.
.TP
.BI \-c " FILE" "\fR, \fP\-\-config " FILE
YAML config file. Default: \fB$SCD_CONFIG\fR, else
\fI~/.config/scd\-reporting/config.yaml\fR. Naming a file that does not exist is an error.
.TP
.BI \-u " URL" "\fR, \fP\-\-url " URL
Server root URL, e.g. \fBhttps://scd\-reporting.fnal.gov\fR.
.TP
.BI \-t " TOKEN" "\fR, \fP\-\-token " TOKEN
API token (Profile \(-> API Token). Prefer \fB\-\-token\-file\fR or the config file:
a token on the command line is visible in the process list and shell history.
.TP
.BI \-\-token\-file " FILE"
Read the token from \fIFILE\fR (used only when no token is set by a higher-priority source).
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " SEC"
Request timeout in seconds (default 300; AI summaries can take minutes).
.TP
.BI \-\-ca\-bundle " FILE"
PEM file of CA certificates used to verify the server.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-insecure
Do not verify the server's TLS certificate. Testing only.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Log each request URL and the response status, type and size to standard error.
The token is never logged.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the client version.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Settings are resolved per key in this order, highest first:
.IP 1. 4
command-line options;
.IP 2. 4
environment variables;
.IP 3. 4
\fB.env\fR files: \fI./.env\fR, then \fI~/.config/scd\-reporting/.env\fR (only \fBSCD_*\fR keys are read;
the current directory's file wins);
.IP 4. 4
the YAML config file;
.IP 5. 4
built-in defaults.
.PP
Config file keys are \fBurl\fR, \fBtoken\fR, \fBtoken_file\fR, \fBtimeout\fR, \fBca_bundle\fR,
\fBinsecure\fR and \fBformat\fR. The file is shared with \fBscd\-post\-entry\fR(1).
Example (see \fIconfig/scd\-client.yaml.example\fR):
.PP
.nf
.RS
url: https://scd\-reporting.fnal.gov
token_file: ~/.config/scd\-reporting/token
format: md
timeout: 300
.RE
.fi
.PP
Run \fBscd\-whoami \-\-settings\fR to see each resolved value and where it came from.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SCD_URL
Server root URL.
.TP
.B SCD_TOKEN
API token.
.TP
.B SCD_TOKEN_FILE
File containing the API token.
.TP
.B SCD_CONFIG
Path of the YAML config file.
.TP
.B SCD_TIMEOUT
Request timeout in seconds.
.TP
.B SCD_CA_BUNDLE
CA certificate bundle.
.TP
.B SCD_INSECURE
\fB1\fR/\fBtrue\fR/\fByes\fR disables TLS verification.
.TP
.B SCD_FORMAT
Default output format of \fBscd\-report\fR(1).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The server rejected the request (HTTP 4xx/5xx). The status and the server's message, including
per-field errors, are printed to standard error. 401 means the token is missing, wrong, revoked
or belongs to a deactivated account; 403 means your role does not allow the request.
.TP
.B 2
Usage or configuration error (no URL or token, bad option, missing config file, binary output to a
terminal).
.TP
.B 3
The server could not be reached (DNS, connection refused, TLS failure, timeout).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/scd\-reporting/config.yaml
Default config file.
.TP
.I ~/.config/scd\-reporting/.env
Per-user \fB.env\fR file.
.TP
.I ./.env
Per-directory \fB.env\fR file.
.SH NOTES
All tools use only the Python standard library (PyYAML is used for the config file when installed,
otherwise a simple \fBkey: value\fR reader). Python 3.9 or later. On Windows run them through the
interpreter, e.g. \fBpy scripts\\scd\-report \-f md\fR or \fBpy scripts\\scd_client.py report \-f md\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
What did I file last month?
.PP
.nf
.RS
scd\-entries \-\-period last\-month
.RE
.fi
.PP
All my NOvA entries as Markdown:
.PP
.nf
.RS
scd\-entries \-p nova \-f md \-o nova.md
.RE
.fi
.PP
Ids of entries tagged timing:
.PP
.nf
.RS
scd\-entries \-q timing \-\-all\-pages \-\-json | jq '.[].id'
.RE
.fi
